,"assignees":[],"milestone":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/milestones/89","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/milestone/89","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/milestones/89/labels","id":4398560,"node_id":"MDk6TWlsZXN0b25lNDM5ODU2MA==","number":89,"title":"1.4.x","description":null,"creator":{"login":"zzzeek","id":128223,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODIyMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128223?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek","html_url":"https://github.com/zzzeek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":0,"closed_issues":522,"state":"open","created_at":"2019-06-11T16:37:26Z","updated_at":"2025-06-19T15:15:28Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":12,"created_at":"2021-10-04T13:26:14Z","updated_at":"2021-10-04T17:20:21Z","closed_at":"2021-10-04T17:20:21Z","author_association":"NONE","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Describe the bug\r\n\r\nWe were surprised with a syntax error when `'ANY(role.zone_ids) IS NULL'` was rendered unexpectedly. The code that generated it used `.filter(sqlalchemy.any_(Role.zone_ids) == some_variable)` which apparently correctly when worked correctly when `some_variable = 5` but rendered with the equal sign flipped when `some_variable = None`.\r\n\r\n\r\n### To Reproduce\r\n\r\nGiven an array column `zone_ids` on table `role`, the expression\r\n\r\n```python\r\nsqlalchemy.any_(Role.zone_ids).is_(None)\r\n```\r\nrenders to `'ANY(role.zone_ids) IS NULL'` fails with `syntax error at or near \"ANY\"` on postgresql.\r\nIt renders correctly when using\r\n```\r\nRole.zone_ids.any(None)\r\n```\r\nwhich renders to `'NULL = ANY (role.zone_ids)'`.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n### Error\r\n\r\n```\r\nSELECT * FROM role WHERE ANY (role.zone_ids) IS NULL;\r\nsyntax error at or near \"ANY\"\r\nLINE 1: SELECT * FROM role WHERE ANY (role.zone_ids) IS NULL\r\n``` \r\n\r\n### Versions\r\n\r\n- OS: ubuntu 16.04\r\n- Python: 3.5\r\n- SQLAlchemy:1.3.24\r\n- Database:Postgresql 13\r\n- DBAPI (eg: psycopg, cx_oracle, mysqlclient): psycopg2\r\n\r\n\r\n### Additional context\r\n\r\nWe found a test for the ANY expression at https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/blob/79a27c9fcb1ba4909834a7e2d51c29afb0688cd5/lib/sqlalchemy/sql/elements.py#L3635 and will contribute a PR if pointed to where it would be correct to implement a fix for this if possible.","closed_by":{"login":"sqlalchemy-bot","id":36047385,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDQ3Mzg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36047385?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/orgs","repos_url":"https://ap